+# Planted inventory
+
+This repository is a smoke target for appsec-review. Everything below is deliberate. The
+evaluation answer key lives in the separate `appsec-review-smoke-guide` repository; this file
+describes the target, it is not the key.
+
+Line numbers refer to the tagged head. The fixture file `lib/synthetic.rb` is byte-identical to
+`tests/fixtures/graph/codeql_export/ruby-synthetic/source/synthetic.rb` in appsec-review, so the
+line numbers its `expected-facts.json` cites are unchanged.
+
+## Build
+
+appsec-review has no Ruby build profile and no catalog image carries a Ruby interpreter, so there
+is no pinned image in which the offline build (`ruby -c lib/*.rb`) can be proved. The syntax check
+was not executed by the Stage 3 verification; it is a recorded gap (appsec-review `docs/TODO.md`
+T-139). Syft, Semgrep, the history checks and the complexity measurement do not need Ruby and
+were run.
+
+## True positives, code
+
+| Id | Weakness | Where | Source to sink |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| TP-C1 | CWE-89 SQL injection | `lib/synthetic.rb` `UsersController#show` | `params[:name]` to `User.find_by_sql` (fixture case `remote_to_sql`) |
+| TP-C2 | CWE-78 command injection | `lib/synthetic.rb` `UsersController#run` | `params[:cmd]` to `system` (fixture case `remote_to_command`, the unguarded call) |
+| TP-C3 | CWE-22 path traversal | `lib/synthetic.rb` `UsersController#read_file` via `CachedStore#fetch` | `params[:path]` to `File.read` (fixture case `remote_to_path`) |
+| TP-C4 | CWE-918 server-side request forgery | `lib/synthetic.rb` `UsersController#download` | `params[:host]` to `Net::HTTP.get` (fixture case `remote_to_ssrf`) |
+| TP-C5 | CWE-502 unsafe deserialization | `lib/synthetic.rb` `UsersController#restore` | `params[:blob]` to `Marshal.load` (fixture case `remote_to_deserialization`) |
+| TP-C6 | CWE-117 log injection | `lib/reports_controller.rb` `ReportsController#show` | `params[:user]` to `Rails.logger.info` |
+| TP-C7 | CWE-601 open redirect | `lib/archive.rb` `ExportsController#done` | `params[:return_to]` to `redirect_to` |
+
+The fixture also carries `UsersController#dispatch_action` (`send(params[:helper])`, an
+unresolved reflective call) and the `ARGV`/`ENV` local sources in `Cli.main`.
+
+## True positives, dependencies
+
+Locked in `Gemfile.lock` and never required by any source file, so the build ignores them while
+SBOM tools that read the lockfile see them.
+
+| Id | Package | Version | Advisory | Fixed in | How present |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| TP-D1 | rack | 2.0.0 | GHSA-5r2p-j47h-mhpg (CVE-2018-16471) | 2.0.6 | direct dependency in `Gemfile` |
+| TP-D2 | sinatra | 2.0.0 | GHSA-h29f-7f56-j8wh (CVE-2018-7212), GHSA-mq35-wqvf-r23c (CVE-2018-11627) | 2.0.1, 2.0.2 | direct dependency in `Gemfile` |
+| TP-D3 | rexml | 3.2.4 | GHSA-8cr8-4vfw-mr7h (CVE-2021-28965) | 3.2.5 | transitive: recorded under `kramdown (2.3.1)` in `Gemfile.lock` only |
+
+rack 2.0.0 also has later advisories (for example CVE-2019-16782, CVE-2020-8161); the planted
+one is the oldest with the lowest fixed version. kramdown 2.3.1, mustermann 1.0.3,
+rack-protection 2.0.0, tilt 2.0.9 and thread_safe 0.3.6 have no OSV record and are not planted.
+
