+
+## False positives
+
+appsec-review mounts no Semgrep rule for Ruby (`rules/semgrep/*.yml` target C, C++ and Java;
+`rules/sei-cert/rules/` has no `ruby` directory), so **no mounted rule reports any of these**.
+They are planted anyway as the constructs a Ruby pattern scanner would flag, each refuted by a
+code-intelligence fact.
+
+| Id | Where | Flagged by | Refuted by |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| FP-1 | `lib/helpers.rb` `Helpers.warm_cache`: `system("bin/true")` | no mounted rule reports it | constant operand: no `dataflow_path` reaches the sink |
+| FP-2 | `lib/helpers.rb` `Helpers.run_tool`: `system(tool)` | no mounted rule reports it | `guard_fact`: `TOOLS.include?(tool)` dominates the sink and constrains its operand |
+| FP-3 | `lib/helpers.rb` `Helpers.read_template`: `File.read(path)` | no mounted rule reports it | `path_sanitizers`: `File.expand_path` with a `start_with?(TEMPLATE_ROOT)` check dominates the sink |
+| FP-4 | `lib/helpers.rb` `Helpers.legacy_dump`: `File.read(path)` | no mounted rule reports it | dead code: no callers, no entry point, so no `dataflow_path` reaches it |
+
+## High-complexity function
+
+`ReportsController#show` in `lib/reports_controller.rb` is the dispatch of the application and
+the function the history touches most. It holds TP-C6. Its intended cyclomatic complexity is above
+15 by the appsec-review counter (branches, loops, `case`/`when` clauses, boolean operators and
+conditional expressions); the measured value is recorded in the guide.
+
+## Code-intelligence cases
+
+`lib/synthetic.rb` carries the appsec-review Ruby graph-export fixture unchanged: the five
+remote-to-sink paths, the `ARGV` and `ENV` local sources, a sanitized path (`File.basename` in
+`Store#fetch`), a dominating and a non-dominating guard (`UsersController#run`), virtual dispatch
+(`store_for(...).fetch`), an unresolved reflective call (`send`) and cross-function flow
+summaries (`CachedStore#fetch`, `Cli.query`). Ruby integers are arbitrary precision, so every
+`ranges` row is `not_applicable`. The fixed state of `read_attachment` adds a `File.basename`
+sanitizer.
+
+## History
+
+Produced by `tools/make-history.sh` from `tools/history/steps/`: 38 commits by three
+synthetic authors, dated 2025-05 to 2026-09, including the introduction and fix of each fixed
+item, a dependency upgrade, a rename (`lib/exports.rb` to `lib/archive.rb`), a revert and its
+reapply, a hardening review that adds `SECURITY.md`, and a commit body that records an
+investigated report found not exploitable (FP-2). Every commit touches at most three files.
